---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import InstallTabs from '../components/InstallTabs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Install" active="install" description="Install all five CLIs in under two minutes — pipx for nda-review-cli, npm for draft-cli, sign-cli, docx2pdf-cli, and compare-cli." toc>
  <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
  <h1>Four installs, one workflow.</h1>

  <p class="text-lg text-ink-700 dark:text-night-100">
    Each CLI is a standalone package on its native registry. Install whichever ones you need;
    they don't depend on each other and there's no shared runtime to set up.
  </p>

  <Callout label="TL;DR">
    <code class="chip">npm i -g @drbaher/draft-cli</code> · <code class="chip">pipx install nda-review-cli</code> · <code class="chip">npm i -g docx2pdf-cli</code> · <code class="chip">npm i -g compare-cli</code> · <code class="chip">npm i -g @drbaher/sign-cli</code>.
    Verify with <code class="chip">--version</code> on each.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Node.js 18+</strong> for draft-cli, sign-cli, and docx2pdf-cli; <strong>Node.js 20+</strong> for compare-cli (pinned by <code class="chip">pdfjs-dist</code>). Install via <code class="chip">brew install node</code>, <code class="chip">nvm</code>, or your platform's installer.</li>
    <li><strong>Python 3.9+</strong> with <code class="chip">pipx</code> for nda-review-cli. Install pipx via <code class="chip">brew install pipx</code> or your distro package manager, then <code class="chip">pipx ensurepath</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>A PDF backend</strong> (only for docx2pdf-cli) — LibreOffice, Microsoft Word, Pandoc, or a Gotenberg server. The tool auto-detects what's installed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>draft-cli</h2>
  <p>
    The Node.js CLI for filling placeholders in markdown or <code class="chip">.docx</code>
    templates. Single-file ESM, one runtime dep (<code class="chip">jszip</code>) for
    <code class="chip">.docx</code> unzip. Installs as <code class="chip">draft</code> on your PATH.
  </p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="draft-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'npm',  label: 'npm',  command: 'npm i -g @drbaher/draft-cli\ndraft --version' },
      { id: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', command: 'pnpm add -g @drbaher/draft-cli' },
      { id: 'yarn', label: 'yarn', command: 'yarn global add @drbaher/draft-cli' },
      { id: 'npx',  label: 'npx',  command: 'npx @drbaher/draft-cli --demo', note: 'No install — runs the bundled NDA demo once.' },
    ]}
  />

  <CodeBlock label="sanity check">{`# See the bundled demo (no template needed)
draft --demo

# Discover what a template expects
draft path/to/template.md --list-placeholders`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>nda-review-cli</h2>
  <p>The Python CLI for drafting, reviewing, and negotiating NDAs. Stdlib-only at runtime — pipx installs it cleanly into its own environment.</p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="nda-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'pipx', label: 'pipx', command: 'pipx install nda-review-cli\nnda-review-cli --version', note: 'Recommended — isolates dependencies and adds the CLI to your $PATH.' },
      { id: 'pip',  label: 'pip',  command: 'pip install --user nda-review-cli', note: 'Use if you don\'t have pipx. Make sure ~/.local/bin is on your $PATH.' },
      { id: 'src',  label: 'from source', command: 'git clone https://github.com/DrBaher/nda-review-cli.git\ncd nda-review-cli && ./nda_review_cli.py --help', note: 'Single-file stdlib-only Python — runs straight from a clone.' },
    ]}
  />

  <CodeBlock label="first-run setup">{`# 16 quick questions write your house policy
nda-review-cli quickstart`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>docx2pdf-cli</h2>
  <p>The Node.js CLI for DOCX → PDF conversion with hybrid backends.</p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="d2p-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'npm',  label: 'npm',  command: 'npm i -g docx2pdf-cli\ndocx2pdf --version' },
      { id: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', command: 'pnpm add -g docx2pdf-cli' },
      { id: 'yarn', label: 'yarn', command: 'yarn global add docx2pdf-cli' },
      { id: 'npx',  label: 'npx',  command: 'npx docx2pdf-cli@latest --doctor', note: 'No install — runs the latest version once.' },
    ]}
  />

  <CodeBlock label="sanity check">{`# Probe what backends are detected on this machine
docx2pdf --doctor
docx2pdf --list-backends`}</CodeBlock>

  <p>
    The <code class="chip">--doctor</code> probe walks every backend candidate (LibreOffice, Word,
    Pandoc, Gotenberg) and reports which ones are usable. Pick one with <code class="chip">--backend</code>
    or let the tool auto-select.
  </p>

  <h2>compare-cli</h2>
  <p>
    The Node.js CLI for clause-aware drift detection between two contract versions. Two runtime
    deps (<code class="chip">jszip</code> + <code class="chip">pdfjs-dist</code>); single-file
    ESM; installs as <code class="chip">compare</code> on your PATH (note: package name and bin
    name differ — see the troubleshooting note below for <code class="chip">npx</code>).
  </p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="compare-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'npm',  label: 'npm',  command: 'npm i -g compare-cli\ncompare --version' },
      { id: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', command: 'pnpm add -g compare-cli' },
      { id: 'yarn', label: 'yarn', command: 'yarn global add compare-cli' },
      { id: 'npx',  label: 'npx',  command: 'npx -p compare-cli@latest -- compare --demo', note: 'No install. The `-p PKG -- BIN` form is required because the package name (`compare-cli`) and bin name (`compare`) differ; npm 10.x\'s `npx` can\'t auto-resolve it.' },
    ]}
  />

  <CodeBlock label="sanity check">{`# Substantive-drift demo against bundled fixtures (deliberately exits 2)
compare --demo

# Same comparison, structured JSON
compare --demo --json | head`}</CodeBlock>

  <p>
    For agent pipelines, the MCP server lives in a separate package:
    <code class="chip">npm i -g compare-cli-mcp</code>. See
    <a href="/built-for-agents/">built for agents</a> for the Claude Desktop / Claude Code
    config snippet.
  </p>

  <h2>sign-cli</h2>
  <p>
    The TypeScript CLI for fully-offline PAdES signing (built-in PKCS#7 signer with a self-issued
    cert) plus optional Dropbox Sign / DocuSign / SignWell routing. Installs as
    <code class="chip">sign</code> on your PATH.
  </p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="sign-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'npm',  label: 'npm',  command: 'npm i -g @drbaher/sign-cli\nsign --version' },
      { id: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', command: 'pnpm add -g @drbaher/sign-cli' },
      { id: 'yarn', label: 'yarn', command: 'yarn global add @drbaher/sign-cli' },
      { id: 'npx',  label: 'npx',  command: 'npx @drbaher/sign-cli demo', note: 'One-shot offline demo — no install required.' },
    ]}
  />

  <p>
    The offline demo walks the full lifecycle (create → approve → send → sign → audit verify →
    bundle export) using the built-in local PAdES signer — no signup, no third-party calls,
    ~5 seconds end to end. After install, run <code class="chip">sign init</code> for a guided
    provider setup or <code class="chip">sign doctor preflight</code> for a structured per-check
    readiness report.
  </p>

  <h2>Configuration locations</h2>
  <p>Each tool keeps its config in standard places. Nothing is shared across tools.</p>
  <table class="not-prose mt-4 w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/15 text-left dark:border-night-300/20">
        <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Tool</th>
        <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Config</th>
        <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Sensitive bits</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="text-ink-700 dark:text-night-100">
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">draft-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">None by default · optional <code class="chip">&lt;template&gt;.params.json</code> alongside the template · optional <code class="chip">parties.json</code> for shared party records</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">LLM provider keys (env only) when <code class="chip">--from-deal</code> is used</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">nda-review-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="chip">config/org-policy.json</code>, <code class="chip">profiles/</code>, optional <code class="chip">config/llm.json</code></td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">LLM provider keys (gitignored)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">docx2pdf-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">Optional <code class="chip">.docx2pdfrc</code></td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">Gotenberg URL if remote backend in use</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">compare-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">None · all behavior driven by flags · for the MCP server, optional <code class="chip">COMPARE_MCP_BASE_DIR</code> env var to lock down path inputs</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">None (no LLM tier, no network)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">sign-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="chip">$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sign-cli/profiles.json</code> (named profile bundles) · project-level <code class="chip">sign-profile.json</code> (git-style upward discovery) · env vars (<code class="chip">SIGN_PROFILE</code>, <code class="chip">SIGN_DB_PATH</code>, etc.)</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">Provider API keys via shell env + <code class="chip">{`{{env:VAR}}`}</code> profile references — credentials never live in the profile file</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Updating</h2>
  <CodeBlock>{`pipx upgrade nda-review-cli
npm update -g @drbaher/draft-cli docx2pdf-cli compare-cli @drbaher/sign-cli`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>Uninstalling</h2>
  <p>
    Each tool comes off cleanly. There are no daemons, services, or system-wide modifications to
    clean up afterwards.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock>{`pipx uninstall nda-review-cli
npm rm -g @drbaher/draft-cli docx2pdf-cli compare-cli @drbaher/sign-cli`}</CodeBlock>
</BaseLayout>
